Clinical truth is fixed. Build the submission only from the supplied `facts` entries. Express every supplied fact and no others. Preserve every positive, explicit negative, measurement, duration, context fact, validity condition, and pre/post-intervention distinction. A field absent from `facts`, null, unknown, or omitted must remain unmentioned: never turn it into a negative, a normal finding, an absence-of-report statement, or an added checklist item.

Treat every fact as an independent protected assertion. A broad parent fact never licenses a narrower child fact. For example, `has_ear_problem=false` permits only a direct no-ear-problem statement and says nothing about discharge, pain, pus, or swelling. `has_fever=true` says nothing about daily fever, eye findings, mouth findings, rash, or bacterial cause unless those facts are supplied separately.

Preserve polarity, connectors, qualifiers, and evidence status exactly:
- positive cough or difficult breathing must remain positive; do not write "no cough or difficult breathing";
- inability to drink or breastfeed must remain inability, while a supplied negative must be rendered directly as ability to drink or breastfeed;
- "drink or breastfeed" must remain OR, never AND;
- diarrhoea-specific drinking status is separate from general danger-sign ability and must be stated independently as normal, eager/thirsty, poorly, or unable when supplied;
- initial wheezing and recurrent wheeze are separate facts; never merge them;
- measurements and durations must retain their exact supplied number and unit;
- a supplied known negative must be direct, never weakened to "not reported", "no history available", or silence;
- "no identified bacterial cause" means none was identified in this assessment, not that no bacterial cause exists;
- malaria risk belongs to the area or setting, not the child;
- preserve caregiver-reported, observed, measured, confirmed, calm-state, full-minute, before-treatment, and after-treatment qualifiers.

Do not add diagnoses, classifications, interpretations, urgency, referral, treatments, advice, summaries, field paths, schema commentary, hashes, rule IDs, policy IDs, or expected outputs.

Return exactly one JSON object matching the supplied candidate schema, containing only `candidate_schema_id`, `semantic_case_id`, `strategy_id`, `user_submission`, and `fact_evidence`. Copy all IDs exactly. `fact_evidence` must contain every supplied `fact_id` exactly once and no other IDs. Each `evidence_text` must be one exact contiguous substring of `user_submission` and must itself preserve the complete fact, including polarity, value, duration, and qualifier. Never use ellipses or reconstructed text.

